# =============================================================================
# SEA-Net -- what does NOT go on GitHub
#
# The public repo is meant to hold three things and nothing else:
#   1. the code            (main.py, seanet/, millet/, configs/, scripts/, notebooks/)
#   2. the results         (results/SEA_NET/, results/paper_figures/, results/UCR/, results/WebTraffic/)
#   3. the built report    (docs/SEA-Net_internship_report.pdf) + README.md
#
# IMPORTANT: adding a path here does NOT remove a file that git already tracks.
# For that you need `git rm -r --cached <path>` once; the file stays on disk.
# =============================================================================

# --- Editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
*~
*#
*.swp
*.DS_Store
/.idea/
/.vscode/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
/.coverage
/.coverage.*
/.cache
/.pytest_cache
/.mypy_cache
/build
/doc/_apidoc/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Our private Telegram bot token + chat id. Never commit this.
scripts/telegram_secrets.sh

# =============================================================================
# BIG OR REGENERABLE DATA
# =============================================================================

# Datasets are provisioned locally, never committed: the UCR 2018 archive
# (~300 MB, own licence) and the synthetic WebTraffic csvs (~19 MB). See the
# README for how to fetch them.
/data/

# Saved model weights: large, and regenerated by training.
/model/
*.pth

# MLflow local tracking store. A database file in git bloats history and causes
# merge conflicts; copy it off the training machine with scp instead.
/mlflow.db
/mlruns/
/mlartifacts/

# Raw per-series probability arrays, ~30 MB across the four multi-seed models.
# Only scripts/ensemble_vote.py reads them, and the result of that script is
# already committed as results/SEA_NET/ensemble_vote.csv and written up in the
# README, so the arrays themselves are not worth 30 MB of repo.
results/SEA_NET/*/predictions/

# Every paper figure is written three times: .pdf (for LaTeX), .png (for the
# README and GitHub) and .svg. The SVG is a pure duplicate of the other two.
results/paper_figures/**/*.svg

# Superseded experiment. The sliding-window results were replaced by the
# per-time-step pipeline in results/SEA_NET/ and nothing cites them any more.
/results/SEA_NET_legacy_slidingwindow/

# Smoke-test outputs. `--smoke` runs are throwaway 3-epoch pipeline checks;
# real training outputs ARE committed, so a run's record travels with the repo.
/results/SEA_NET/*/logs/smoke/
/results/SEA_NET/*/interpretation/*/smoke/
/results/SEA_NET/logs/smoke/

# Raw Grid'5000 job dumps: the console output of a training run (one file was
# 23 MB) that nothing reads back. The numbers are already in results.csv.
# logs/ is recreated by scripts/run_all.sh and scripts/launch.sh (both mkdir -p).
/OAR.*.stdout
/OAR.*.stderr
/logs/

# JVM crash dumps left behind by a tool that died. Pure noise.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# =============================================================================
# THE REPORT
# =============================================================================
# The LaTeX sources of the internship report are kept private. Only the built
# PDF is published, as docs/SEA-Net_internship_report.pdf, so that a reader who
# arrives from the report's own link can find it again.
/ICLR_2025_Report/

# LaTeX build leftovers from the architecture slides. The three archi_level*.png
# images ARE committed, because the README embeds them.
model_architecture/*.aux
model_architecture/*.bbl
model_architecture/*.blg
model_architecture/*.log
model_architecture/*.out
model_architecture/*.synctex.gz
model_architecture/*.toc
model_architecture/*.fls
model_architecture/*.fdb_latexmk
model_architecture/*.nav
model_architecture/*.snm
model_architecture/*.vrb

# Old, abandoned draft. Superseded by ICLR_2025_Report/ and then by docs/.
/report/
/Latex/

# pdflatex writes texput.log when started with no file name at all.
texput.log

# =============================================================================
# PRIVATE WORKING NOTES
# =============================================================================
# These are my own notes for running the project, not documentation for anyone
# else. Everything a reader needs is in README.md.
CLAUDE.md
PROJECT_STATE.md
workflow.md
GIT_GUIDE.md
GRID5K_CMD_HELP.md
MLFLOW_GUIDE.md
CLUSTER_REQ_CMD.md
CLUSTERS_CMD.md
README_OLD.md
MILLET_Overview.png
text papers/
